.TH ECL_CLIENT 3 "2026-09-23" "ecl-client 1.0.0" "Python Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ecl_client \- Python interface to the Fermilab Electronic Logbook client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B import ecl_client as ecl
.PP
.BI "entry = ecl.Entry(" category )
.BI "client = ecl.Client(" url ", " username ", " password ", " auth_mode "=ecl.AuthMode.XML_SIGNATURE)"
.BI "result = client.post(" entry )
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ecl_client
is a pybind11 extension over the C++ library documented in
.BR ecl (3).
It is distributed as the
.B fnal-ecl-client
package and requires Python 3.9 or newer.
.SS Enumerations
.TP
.B AuthMode
.BR XML_SIGNATURE ", " PASSWORD .
.TP
.B TextFormat
.BR PLAIN ", " TEXTILE ", " PREFORMATTED .
.SS Entry(category)
All methods except
.B xml
return the entry, so calls can be chained.
.TP
.BI subject( value ") , text(" value ") , form(" value )
.TP
.BI format( TextFormat )
.TP
.BI private_entry( value =True)
.TP
.BI related( entry_id )
.TP
.BI tag( value )
.TP
.BI field( name ", " value )
.TP
.BI attachment( name ", " path ") , image(" name ", " path )
Read the file when called.
.TP
.BI attachment_data( name ", " filename ", " data ") , image_data(" name ", " filename ", " data )
.I data
is a bytes-like object.
.TP
.B xml()
Serialised XML; also returned by
.BR str() .
.SS Client(url, username, password, auth_mode)
.TP
.BI timeout( seconds ") , connect_timeout(" seconds )
.TP
.BI tls_verify( enabled ") , user_agent(" value )
.TP
.BI post( entry )
Returns a
.BR PostResult .
The GIL is released for the network operation, so posts from several threads
proceed concurrently, provided each thread uses its own
.BR Client .
.SS PostResult
Read-only attributes
.BR http_status ", " entry_id ", " response_body ", " effective_url ,
and property
.BR created .
.SS instance_url(name)
Returns
.BI https://dbweb0.fnal.gov/ECL/ name\fR,
or
.I name
unchanged if it contains
.BR :// .
.SH ERRORS
Library failures raise
.BR ecl_client.ECLError ,
a subclass of
.BR Exception .
Invalid argument values raise
.B ECLError
from the setter that received them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
import os
import ecl_client as ecl

entry = (ecl.Entry("Sandbox")
         .subject("Python post")
         .text("Automated entry")
         .tag("automated")
         .attachment("report", "report.txt"))
client = ecl.Client(ecl.instance_url("mu2e"),
                    os.environ["ECL_USERNAME"],
                    os.environ["ECL_PASSWORD"],
                    ecl.AuthMode.PASSWORD)
r = client.post(entry)
print(r.entry_id, r.effective_url)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ecl-post (1),
.BR ecl (3)
